course: dictionary
lesson: 10769
title: UTC, the world clock
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Clocks in different countries do not always show the same time, so the world needs one shared clock to measure from. That clock is UTC, short for Coordinated Universal Time. Other places are then given a time zone, written as UTC plus or minus some hours.
explain: Context clues help you here. «Italy in summer is 2 hours ahead of UTC, so 18:00 UTC is 20:00 in Italy.» Ahead tells you Italy's clock shows a later time, so you add 2 hours: 18:00 becomes 20:00.
explain: Behind works the other way round. If a place is behind UTC, you take hours away. In winter, UTC is the same as the time in London, so a clock in London in January shows the same time as UTC.
fact: UTC stands for Coordinated Universal Time.
fact: UTC is the main world time standard that clocks and computers use.
fact: Time zones are written as UTC+10 or UTC−5, meaning 10 hours ahead or 5 hours behind.
fact: Pilots, scientists and weather forecasters use UTC so that everyone means the same time.
fact: In the UK, UTC can also mean a University Technical College, but in time lessons it means the world clock.
exercise: What does UTC stand for? | Universal Time Zone Clock | *Coordinated Universal Time | United Time Clock Company
exercise: If a place is UTC−5, what does the −5 tell you? | It is the same as UTC | It is 5 minutes ahead of UTC | *It is 5 hours behind UTC | It is 5 hours ahead of UTC
exercise: In winter, UTC is the same as the time in which place? | New York | *London, which uses Greenwich Mean Time | Paris | Sydney
test: «Italy in summer is 2 hours ahead of UTC.» If it is 18:00 UTC, what time is it in Italy? | 16:00 | *20:00 | 18:02 | 17:00
test: New York is several hours behind UTC. Does its clock show a later or an earlier time than UTC? | *Earlier | Exactly midnight | The same | Later
exam: A ship's clock shows 09:00 UTC and the place it reaches is UTC+3. What is the local time? | 09:03 | *12:00 | 15:00 | 06:00
